{#-
  Swiss (CH) print/PDF layout.  Self-contained: no JS, no network requests, one
  language -- same contract as print.html.j2, whose CSS and block structure this
  deliberately follows so the two stay easy to diff.

  Why a separate template at all: a Swiss application dossier is structurally
  different from the generic A4 CV, not just differently worded.

    * A photo is conventional and expected (meta.photo).
    * A "Personal details" block carries nationality/citizenship and work-permit
      status up front, where a Swiss screener looks for it.
    * Date of birth is conventional in Switzerland.  It is NOT in data/cv.yaml
      and must not be invented, so the block renders that row only if the field
      ``meta.date_of_birth`` ever appears in the data (read straight off
      ``variant.data`` -- see the comment at the row itself).
    * Languages are listed with their CEFR level, exactly as recorded.
    * "References available on request" (plus the Arbeitszeugnis note) closes the
      dossier: Swiss employers expect referees and a work certificate, but those
      are supplied on request, not printed here.
    * No salary expectations anywhere -- these belong in the cover letter, if
      asked for at all, never in the CV.
    * Education states the coursework-only position explicitly via
      ``ui.coursework_only``; there is no degree to claim and no equivalence
      statement to make.

  Restraint is the point: Swiss screeners read this, designers do not.
-#}
{#-
  Static, user-visible chrome that has no home in data/cv.yaml.  build.py keeps
  such strings bilingual in its UI_STRINGS table; that table lives in build.py,
  which this variant may not extend, so the same {en, cs} pattern is applied
  locally here instead.  `lang` is guaranteed to be 'en' or 'cs' (build.py
  validates ``locale``), so it indexes these maps directly.
-#}
{% set chrome = {
  'personal_details': {'en': 'Personal details', 'cs': 'Osobní údaje'},
  'nationality':      {'en': 'Nationality', 'cs': 'Státní příslušnost'},
  'work_permit':      {'en': 'Work permit', 'cs': 'Pracovní povolení'},
  'date_of_birth':    {'en': 'Date of birth', 'cs': 'Datum narození'},
  'residence':        {'en': 'Place of residence', 'cs': 'Bydliště'},
  'references':       {'en': 'References', 'cs': 'Reference'},
  'references_line':  {
    'en': 'References available on request — two to three referees and work certificates (Arbeitszeugnisse) can be provided on request.',
    'cs': 'Reference na vyžádání — dva až tři referenti a pracovní posudky (Arbeitszeugnis) k dispozici na vyžádání.'
  }
} %}
{#- Raw merged data, used only for fields build.py does not lift into `meta`. -#}
{% set raw_meta = (variant.data.get('meta') or {}) %}
<!-- {{ generated_note }} -->
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ lang }}">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>{{ meta.name }} — CV ({{ variant.name }})</title>
<style>
{% raw %}
/* Sized to hold the dossier to exactly two A4 pages -- the Swiss norm, and a
   budget build.py asserts.  Type is a touch smaller than print.html.j2's. */
@page { size: A4; margin: 12mm 14mm 11mm 14mm; }
* { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
html { font-size: 8.2pt; }
body {
  font-family: "DejaVu Sans", "Liberation Sans", Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  color: #111;
  background: #fff;
  line-height: 1.3;
}
a { color: #14506e; text-decoration: none; }

/* --- header: photo + identity, the conventional Swiss opening ------------ */
header.cv-head { border-bottom: 2px solid #14506e; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-bottom: 8px; display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start; }
.cv-head img { width: 82px; height: 82px; border-radius: 3px; object-fit: cover; border: 1px solid #b9c6ce; flex: none; }
.cv-head-text { flex: 1; }
h1 { font-size: 1.74rem; line-height: 1.12; margin-bottom: 2px; color: #14506e; }
.headline { font-size: 0.96rem; font-weight: bold; }
.tagline { font-size: 0.91rem; font-style: italic; color: #444; }
.contact { font-size: 0.87rem; margin-top: 3px; color: #333; }
.contact span.sep { color: #999; padding: 0 3px; }

/* --- personal-details block --------------------------------------------- */
.personal { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 2px 14px; font-size: 0.89rem; margin-bottom: 7px; }
.personal .pd { flex: 0 0 auto; }
.personal .pd b { color: #14506e; font-weight: bold; }

h2 {
  font-size: 1.09rem; color: #14506e; margin-top: 7px; margin-bottom: 3px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid #cfd9e0; padding-bottom: 1px;
  page-break-after: avoid; break-after: avoid;
}
h3 { font-size: 0.98rem; margin-bottom: 1px; page-break-after: avoid; break-after: avoid; }
p { margin-bottom: 2px; }
ul { margin: 1px 0 3px 14px; }
li { margin-bottom: 1px; }
.job, .project, .edu { margin-bottom: 5px; page-break-inside: avoid; break-inside: avoid; }
.job-meta, .meta { font-size: 0.87rem; color: #555; margin-bottom: 2px; }
.emphasized { font-weight: bold; }
.tags { font-size: 0.80rem; color: #666; margin-top: 1px; }
.project.compact { font-size: 0.89rem; margin-bottom: 3px; }
.project.compact .sep { color: #999; padding: 0 2px; }
.skill-groups { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0 16px; }
.skill-group { flex: 1 1 46%; min-width: 46%; page-break-inside: avoid; break-inside: avoid; }
.skill-row { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 5px; font-size: 0.89rem; margin-bottom: 0.5px; }
.skill-row .name { flex: 1; }
.skill-row .level { color: #666; font-size: 0.83rem; flex: none; }
.inline-list { font-size: 0.91rem; }
.references { font-size: 0.91rem; }
footer.cv-foot { margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 3px; border-top: 1px solid #cfd9e0; font-size: 0.80rem; color: #666; }
{% endraw %}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header class="cv-head">
  {% if meta.photo %}
  {# Professional photo: conventional in a Swiss dossier, unusual elsewhere. #}
  <img src="{{ meta.photo }}" alt="{{ meta.photo_alt }}">
  {% endif %}
  <div class="cv-head-text">
    <h1>{{ meta.name }}</h1>
    <div class="headline">{{ meta.headline }}</div>
    {% if meta.tagline %}<div class="tagline">{{ meta.tagline }}</div>{% endif %}
    <div class="contact">
      {% for link in meta.contact_links %}
      {{ link.label }}: <a href="{{ link.href }}">{{ link.short }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}<span class="sep">|</span>{% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

{#- Personal details: nationality and permit status where a Swiss reader expects
    them.  Date of birth is conventional here but absent from data/cv.yaml; it is
    read off the raw data so that adding `meta.date_of_birth:` to the YAML is all
    it takes to render the row, and nothing is invented until then. -#}
<div class="personal">
  {% if meta.citizenship %}
  <span class="pd"><b>{{ chrome.nationality[lang] }}:</b> {{ meta.citizenship }}</span>
  {% endif %}
  {% if raw_meta.get('date_of_birth') %}
  <span class="pd"><b>{{ chrome.date_of_birth[lang] }}:</b> {{ raw_meta.get('date_of_birth') }}</span>
  {% endif %}
  {% if meta.city %}
  <span class="pd"><b>{{ chrome.residence[lang] }}:</b> {{ meta.city }}{% if meta.country %}, {{ meta.country }}{% endif %}</span>
  {% endif %}
  {% if work_authorization %}
  <span class="pd"><b>{{ chrome.work_permit[lang] }}:</b> {{ work_authorization }}</span>
  {% endif %}
</div>

{% for section in sections %}
{#- The availability/work-authorization section is folded into the personal
    details block above, so it is not repeated as a section of its own. -#}
{% if section.id not in ['contact', 'availability'] %}
<h2>{{ section.title }}</h2>

{% if section.id == 'summary' %}
  {% for line in summary %}<p>{{ line }}</p>{% endfor %}

{% elif section.id == 'preferred_roles' %}
  <ul>
    {% for role in preferred_roles %}
    <li{% if role.emphasized %} class="emphasized"{% endif %}>{{ role.text }}{% if role.note %} — {{ role.note }}{% endif %}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>

{% elif section.id == 'experience' %}
  {#- Reverse-chronological, as the master data already is.  Dates are shown as
      the data holds them; an entry whose dates are still the TODO(user)
      sentinel renders with no range at all (build.py's fmt_period), which is
      deliberate and asserted -- never a guessed date. -#}
  {% for job in experience %}
  <div class="job">
    <h3>{{ job.role }}</h3>
    <div class="job-meta">{{ job.company }}{% if job.via %} ({{ ui.via }} {{ job.via }}){% endif %}{% if job.period %} &middot; {{ job.period }}{% endif %}</div>
    <p>{{ job.summary }}</p>
    {% if job.highlights %}
    <ul>
      {% for hl in job.highlights %}
      <li{% if hl.emphasized %} class="emphasized"{% endif %}>{{ hl.text }}</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}

{% elif section.id == 'skills' %}
  <div class="skill-groups">
    {% for group in skills %}
    <div class="skill-group">
      <h3>{{ group.title }}</h3>
      {% for item in group['items'] %}
      {#- Plain level labels, no progress bars: a self-scored bar chart reads as
          decoration to a Swiss screener. -#}
      <div class="skill-row">
        <span class="name">{{ item.name }}</span>
        <span class="level">{{ item.level_label }}</span>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

{% elif section.id == 'open_source' %}
  {#- One compact entry per project: name, reach, stack and URL.  The long
      project descriptions from the data are left to the online version linked
      in the footer -- two A4 pages is the Swiss budget, and the work history
      has the stronger claim on the space. -#}
  {% for project in open_source %}
  <div class="project compact">
    <strong>{{ project.name }}</strong>{% if project.stars is not none %} — {{ project.stars }} {{ ui.stars }}{% if project.forks is not none %}, {{ project.forks }} {{ ui.forks }}{% endif %}{% endif %}
    <span class="sep">|</span> <a href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.url | replace('https://', '') }}</a>
    {% if project.tech %}<div class="tags">{{ project.tech | join(' · ') }}</div>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}

{% elif section.id == 'education' %}
  {#- ui.coursework_only states the no-degree position in words. No degree was
      awarded, so there is nothing to have recognised abroad either: no SERI /
      swissuniversities equivalence line belongs here, and build.py's
      assert_no_degree_claim fails the build if one appears. -#}
  {% for item in education %}
  <div class="edu">
    <strong>{{ item.institution }}</strong> — {{ item.field }}{% if item.period %} &middot; {{ item.period }}{% endif %}<br>
    {% if not item.degree_awarded %}<em>{{ ui.coursework_only }}</em>{% if item.note %} — {% endif %}{% endif %}
    {% if item.note %}{{ item.note }}{% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}

{% elif section.id == 'languages' %}
  {#- CEFR levels exactly as recorded in the data, including the weak ones.
      Overstating German in a Swiss application is found out at the interview. -#}
  <p class="inline-list">{% for language in languages %}{{ language.name }} ({{ language.cefr }}){% if not loop.last %} &middot; {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>

{% elif section.id == 'interests' %}
  <p class="inline-list">{% for interest in interests %}{{ interest }}{% if not loop.last %} &middot; {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>

{% elif section.id == 'testimonials' %}
  {% for item in testimonials %}
  <p>“{{ item.quote }}” — {{ item.attribution }}</p>
  {% endfor %}
{% endif %}

{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{#- Closing convention: referees and Arbeitszeugnisse on request.  No names,
    no contact details and no salary expectations are printed. -#}
<h2>{{ chrome.references[lang] }}</h2>
<p class="references">{{ chrome.references_line[lang] }}</p>

<footer class="cv-foot">
  {{ ui.online_version }}: <a href="{{ site_url }}">{{ site_url }}</a>
  &middot; &copy; {{ meta.name }}. {{ ui.rights }}
</footer>

</body>
</html>
